{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>At the appointed time it will be said to Jacob.</b> At this appointed time. And the sense is: at every time it will be said to them, without the knowledge of augury." "<b>What God has wrought.</b> What El will work. And the word [referring to the future tense] is [used] in the past tense (עבר) because everything is decreed, and if it is for the future, it has already been decreed from the beginning. And he says this to Israel by way of prophecy, which is truth." "<b>To Jacob and to Israel.</b> A doubled expression in prophecy, like 'from the peak of Senir and Hermon.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:12.615648186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}